1
00:00:01,490 --> 00:00:03,770
Please introduce yourself

2
00:00:05,270 --> 00:00:07,790
I'm Bhavagna. I am a member of CCF

3
00:00:08,410 --> 00:00:10,410
and I am in third year

4
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:10,950
Okay

5
00:00:11,470 --> 00:00:14,950
So Bhavagna what prompted you to join CCF?

6
00:00:16,670 --> 00:00:18,350
Just the

7
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:19,730
love for animals

8
00:00:20,510 --> 00:00:23,790
Also dogs or cats, I just loved contributing

9
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:27,230
In general yeah

10
00:00:27,230 --> 00:00:29,530
okay, and it started

11
00:00:29,530 --> 00:00:33,550
It didn't really start as me applying for something.

12
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:41,830
When I was in Sarojini, there's this group of people who I saw that were feeding the dogs

13
00:00:41,830 --> 00:00:46,750
and through connections I got to know them

14
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:55,530
And then one day they just recommended people in the WhatsApp group to CCS

15
00:00:56,730 --> 00:01:03,830
I think it was first year SEM break. That's when people called and asked for enrollment numbers

16
00:01:03,830 --> 00:01:05,990
And that is how it became official

17
00:01:06,710 --> 00:01:13,330
And I don't really work under CCF, its more like the Sarojini sector of it

18
00:01:13,330 --> 00:01:17,830
Every Bhavan has their own volunteers who do the feeding

19
00:01:17,830 --> 00:01:25,090
and take care of the dogs, medication, winter coats, stuff like that.

20
00:01:26,210 --> 00:01:29,430
So you're responsible for Sarojini's part of the dogs?

21
00:01:31,870 --> 00:01:33,790
Why do you think...

22
00:01:34,370 --> 00:01:37,770
What do you think about the huge controversy that is going on

23
00:01:37,770 --> 00:01:41,510
where so many people are against having dogs on campus at all?

24
00:01:41,690 --> 00:01:46,150
I get their side as well because dogs are disruptive

25
00:01:48,010 --> 00:01:57,830
Especially since December of last year, I've learned from a problem that there have been like five rabies cases

26
00:01:57,830 --> 00:02:02,710
and at one point in time the hospital didn't even have enough rabies vaccine to give them.

27
00:02:04,150 --> 00:02:08,210
I think the major issue is that dogs don't get enough food outside

28
00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:10,710
That's why they come inside of bowens in order to get food

29
00:02:10,710 --> 00:02:12,830
They don't really have any other motive.

30
00:02:13,250 --> 00:02:14,810
I feel even in Himalaya,

31
00:02:15,710 --> 00:02:18,210
the dog issue is huge.

32
00:02:18,650 --> 00:02:22,890
They just come and go through the dustbins or drink water.

33
00:02:22,970 --> 00:02:26,310
This doesn't happen in Sarojini because

34
00:02:26,310 --> 00:02:28,450
the dogs are fed everyday

35
00:02:29,310 --> 00:02:30,650
both by volunteers

36
00:02:30,650 --> 00:02:33,930
and by ECCF members who come.

37
00:02:34,330 --> 00:02:36,670
In Kasturbaai it doesn't happen

38
00:02:36,670 --> 00:02:40,370
because there is a dog outside guarding and not letting the other dog in.

39
00:02:40,650 --> 00:02:44,070
And also, because the bovins have very small entrances

40
00:02:44,070 --> 00:02:46,530
and it's easier to manage with Himalaya

41
00:02:46,530 --> 00:02:48,890
It's just that walls are very low

42
00:02:48,890 --> 00:02:56,090
and then the guard is not always present at the huge entrance like there is

43
00:02:56,090 --> 00:02:57,690
The issue is just food

44
00:02:59,190 --> 00:03:02,530
With the dog biting issue

45
00:03:02,530 --> 00:03:06,170
I think it's not the dogs on campus mostly

46
00:03:06,670 --> 00:03:10,310
I've also had a dog attack on me near Kasturba.

47
00:03:10,850 --> 00:03:13,570
When first year, I was going to NCC camp

48
00:03:13,570 --> 00:03:15,570
for no reason they just started barking

49
00:03:16,150 --> 00:03:19,190
and even fell down the guard had to come and help me

50
00:03:19,190 --> 00:03:20,190
They didn't bite me but

51
00:03:20,710 --> 00:03:23,930
there were...they did have a reputation of being aggressive

52
00:03:23,930 --> 00:03:25,290
The dogs near sack

53
00:03:25,290 --> 00:03:28,570
And there were also reported cases of dog biting

54
00:03:28,570 --> 00:03:29,410
Near sack

55
00:03:29,410 --> 00:03:30,170
By either of us

56
00:03:30,170 --> 00:03:30,530
Yeah

57
00:03:31,010 --> 00:03:34,090
I think those are the only group of dogs that actually bite people

58
00:03:34,870 --> 00:03:35,830
On campus

59
00:03:36,910 --> 00:03:39,530
That and near Mac also, is it cool?

60
00:03:40,310 --> 00:03:41,070
I don't think so.

61
00:03:41,970 --> 00:03:46,770
The ones near Mandir, there were two cases of biting near Mandir.

62
00:03:47,390 --> 00:03:48,050
So maybe that.

63
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:53,650
I think the major dog bites are from dogs which come from outside.

64
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:57,070
Since there are female dogs on campus they go into heat

65
00:03:57,070 --> 00:03:59,490
And during that time many dogs come from outside

66
00:03:59,490 --> 00:04:03,150
They see that there's availability of food here

67
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:08,490
Since I have been feeding Sarojini, I think two dogs have added since.

68
00:04:09,290 --> 00:04:12,770
And those are big dogs and they're not neutered or vaccinated.

69
00:04:12,990 --> 00:04:14,310
If C-chef does find a new dog,

70
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:16,310
They make sure that it gets neutered

71
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:18,670
if you see the cut on the ear

72
00:04:18,670 --> 00:04:20,710
It means that they've been vaccinated

73
00:04:20,710 --> 00:04:25,310
So even with the bite there is no high chance of contacting any disease

74
00:04:25,310 --> 00:04:27,870
but obviously you'll have to go get a vaccine

75
00:04:28,610 --> 00:04:29,630
To not take any chances

76
00:04:29,630 --> 00:04:31,770
Does C-chef plan to vaccinate those dogs?

77
00:04:31,770 --> 00:04:32,370
or what?

78
00:04:33,150 --> 00:04:38,270
If we find a new dog, we do make sure to get the vet in and take care.

79
00:04:39,370 --> 00:04:45,230
So do you think this dog biting issue can be solved if the manpower of people feeding

80
00:04:45,230 --> 00:04:48,850
the dogs is increased like all their dogs are just properly fed?

81
00:04:50,030 --> 00:04:59,470
To an extent I think so but also need to control the entry and exit of dogs because most of

82
00:04:59,470 --> 00:05:02,470
The dogs that come inside usually leave.

83
00:05:04,210 --> 00:05:10,170
Due to the availability of food and scarcity outside, they stay back.

84
00:05:10,630 --> 00:05:13,610
We can't feed every dog in Roorkee.

85
00:05:15,370 --> 00:05:17,310
These dogs are also territorial.

86
00:05:18,210 --> 00:05:21,950
I told you two dogs have added up in Sarosha.

87
00:05:22,650 --> 00:05:24,470
Those two dogs still don't fit in.

88
00:05:24,470 --> 00:05:31,630
There is basically the group, the dog group and it's their leader most probably a female.

89
00:05:33,350 --> 00:05:38,630
And there are tensions always between this leader or the members of the group to the new additions.

90
00:05:39,770 --> 00:05:42,470
Since we go to feeding they don't do anything to us

91
00:05:42,470 --> 00:05:46,410
They're very frightful if you just say their name or point a stick

92
00:05:46,410 --> 00:05:49,930
They listen. But the others don't know that.

93
00:05:51,190 --> 00:05:57,370
When we are trying to feed them, their attention is coming near the bowls or shouting or barking.

94
00:05:58,350 --> 00:06:03,310
So people see this and think these dogs are aggressive which is just them being territorial.

95
00:06:04,670 --> 00:06:10,590
For them it's kind of valid but if you see from outside it seems like they're rogues and they're just trying to...

96
00:06:11,910 --> 00:06:14,610
and barking at cars or bikes.

97
00:06:15,110 --> 00:06:17,630
If the car or bike stop, they don't bark because

98
00:06:17,630 --> 00:06:20,130
I told you stupid and dumb

99
00:06:20,130 --> 00:06:21,990
They don't do anything

100
00:06:23,030 --> 00:06:26,210
You can't just say to people who are afraid of dogs

101
00:06:26,210 --> 00:06:27,950
that they don't do anything

102
00:06:27,950 --> 00:06:28,990
and expect them to be like

103
00:06:28,990 --> 00:06:30,830
OMG, it's going to be fine

104
00:06:30,830 --> 00:06:32,130
You can't just expect that

105
00:06:32,130 --> 00:06:33,990
I understand two sides of this issue

106
00:06:33,990 --> 00:06:36,430
but again we will have to consider

107
00:06:36,430 --> 00:06:39,670
if we are in a campus

108
00:06:40,670 --> 00:06:43,810
We also have to recognize that they belong here too.

109
00:06:45,810 --> 00:06:49,310
There is no issue with cats because they don't usually come out of bubbles.

110
00:06:50,350 --> 00:06:54,690
Majorly the dustbin issue, the toppling of dustbins was due to cats

111
00:06:54,690 --> 00:06:56,890
Because those are the only ones who live inside

112
00:06:56,890 --> 00:06:59,290
They don't go outside because they do the dog killing

113
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:08,590
It's just the feed, they eat food but sometimes they get greedy and want more food

114
00:07:08,590 --> 00:07:11,610
We can't do anything about that issue.

115
00:07:13,330 --> 00:07:24,010
I feel like the prof who told me about this, in AV's cases, allegedly when I talked about these cases and the group they were like

116
00:07:24,010 --> 00:07:29,450
nothing like this actually happened but he is a professor so we will have to give weight for his word

117
00:07:29,450 --> 00:07:33,330
And since it's during holidays, we don't know what actually happened.

118
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:41,150
Even he told me that there are plans about a new shelter outside of campus.

119
00:07:42,650 --> 00:07:50,910
They're constructing this huge shelter so they could just take every dog from campus and put them in the shelter.

120
00:07:51,590 --> 00:07:52,970
Where will the shelter be?

121
00:07:53,430 --> 00:07:57,290
No idea! It'll be constructed not very soon but someday.

122
00:07:57,290 --> 00:08:03,580
And we have some other sources confirming this as well.

123
00:08:05,810 --> 00:08:07,390
We most probably think that it is happening.

124
00:08:09,550 --> 00:08:18,010
Since Uttarakhand High Court gave similar ruling to Delhi High Court about the dog issue and things,

125
00:08:18,450 --> 00:08:26,050
you can look at Karakpur dog issues even the professor suggested that we look into Karakpur IIT.

126
00:08:27,290 --> 00:08:32,670
The way they solve this issue, even they put the meshes on before every boven.

127
00:08:32,890 --> 00:08:36,950
Restricting the entry space and things like that so that dogs don't come in.

128
00:08:37,130 --> 00:08:48,970
I think Roorkee did take inspiration from that because we did suggest from CCF site to look into it.

129
00:08:48,970 --> 00:08:55,290
The issue is that it's a good solution to just take every animal from here and give them shelter and food.

130
00:08:55,690 --> 00:09:00,750
But the issue is, shelter cannot accommodate many animals

131
00:09:00,750 --> 00:09:02,970
And they will put animals down

132
00:09:03,610 --> 00:09:08,770
It's like anywhere if they don't get enough food or there isn't enough space

133
00:09:08,770 --> 00:09:10,950
They'll just put animals down for no reason

134
00:09:11,690 --> 00:09:15,230
That's the only thing that SheSafe has an issue with

135
00:09:15,230 --> 00:09:16,730
Like they don't need to be put down

136
00:09:17,330 --> 00:09:18,670
Yeah, of course

137
00:09:18,970 --> 00:09:25,250
I think that's the only thing. There are good arguments on both sides but

138
00:09:25,250 --> 00:09:31,190
I guess we'll have to live with it or find better solutions to deal with this

139
00:09:31,190 --> 00:09:34,810
Yeah, I had another question which I think has been neutralized now

140
00:09:34,810 --> 00:09:39,950
I was going to ask that usually people who are very fond of dogs

141
00:09:40,930 --> 00:09:44,610
They've never in person experienced a first hand dog attack

142
00:09:44,610 --> 00:09:45,850
I don't think so.

143
00:09:46,290 --> 00:09:49,770
I mean, I've been chased by four dogs.

144
00:09:49,770 --> 00:09:51,950
That still didn't change your opinion about them?

145
00:09:53,770 --> 00:10:01,270
I think you can quote Steve Irwin if an animal attacks me it's my fault we're not the animals

146
00:10:01,270 --> 00:10:05,090
and I don't think its true in the dog's case because

147
00:10:05,090 --> 00:10:06,490
If the victim is blaming then

148
00:10:07,750 --> 00:10:12,650
In Roorkee even outside I went to see Nisra

149
00:10:12,650 --> 00:10:14,530
That's why I'm living here, right?

150
00:10:14,690 --> 00:10:20,690
So, I went outside to his house and then two dogs chased me.

151
00:10:21,430 --> 00:10:22,230
The outside ones.

152
00:10:23,150 --> 00:10:24,850
The issue with dogs is that they are territorial

153
00:10:24,850 --> 00:10:26,630
And also very scared

154
00:10:28,530 --> 00:10:30,930
They tend to attack them

155
00:10:31,650 --> 00:10:32,870
To defend themselves

156
00:10:32,870 --> 00:10:35,410
But that doesn't instill a fear in you

157
00:10:35,410 --> 00:10:39,150
It does, it doesn't mean I am not afraid of dogs

158
00:10:39,150 --> 00:10:43,430
They just make sure to not get in their business or not look them eye-in-eye.

159
00:10:43,890 --> 00:10:45,430
But sometimes it happens.

160
00:10:47,370 --> 00:10:54,050
And as far as me, people in the group Sarojini Group, they have been a bit as well like

161
00:10:54,050 --> 00:10:56,810
they had to get vaccines and stuff like that.

162
00:10:57,110 --> 00:10:58,430
It's just that it happens and

163
00:10:59,610 --> 00:11:03,530
People just move on or try to understand from their perspective.

164
00:11:05,230 --> 00:11:10,010
It's not that people who love animals don't have bad experiences with them.

165
00:11:10,130 --> 00:11:16,070
I think most of those people do have a lot of experience because they are the ones spending more clothes.

166
00:11:16,410 --> 00:11:22,730
Yeah, makes sense. Is there anything else you would like to say to dog haters or anti-dog people on campus?

167
00:11:23,110 --> 00:11:25,730
I can only urge them to look from the other side.

168
00:11:26,030 --> 00:11:27,870
Yeah, have some empathy.

169
00:11:29,850 --> 00:11:32,750
Okay, I think we're good. Thanks!

